        {
          "step": "opening",
          "proposals": 1,
          "location": "The Burning Wizard, Beregost",
          "actors": 1,
          "droppedPcActors": [],
          "narration": "Late afternoon light slants through the shutters of the Burning Wizard, and the smell of hearth smoke and small beer hangs over the common room. Three travellers have come in by three roads and found the same table. Bram Halloway walked up the Coast Way from Nashkel with the dust of the road still on his boots. Sefa Marrin came up from Baldur's Gate by the Trade Way. Pell Dunmore arrived from the west by the High Hedge road. None of them knows the others yet, and each has reasons for being here that the others have not heard. Behind the bar, the proprietor Doran Quill sets down a cup and looks from one face to the next, as if waiting to see who will speak first. Outside, the forge hammers have fallen silent for the day, and the street beyond the shutters is going dim. What happens at this table is still undecided.",
          "questions": [],
          "startMinutes": 840
